{% extends "bear/_manage.html" %}
{% block title %}{{ hat.name }} · Hats{% endblock %}
{% block manage %}
<p><a href="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats">← All hats</a></p>
<div class="box">
  <h2>{{ hat.name | e }}</h2>
  {% if message %}<p>{{ message | e }}</p>{% endif %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}">
    <label>Responsibility <input name="name" value="{{ hat.name | e }}" required maxlength="120"></label>
    <label>Purpose <textarea name="purpose" required rows="3">{{ hat.purpose | e }}</textarea></label>
    <label>Hat identity text <textarea name="identity_prompt" required rows="5" maxlength="4000">{{ hat.identity_prompt | e }}</textarea></label>
    <p class="form-hint">Hat-specific identity for future conversations and authorized Work wearing this hat. It does not grant tools, credentials, or permissions; Bear-wide identity and execution rules stay separate. Earlier custom stance instructions are not automatically copied into hats; review them before relying on a new identity.</p>
    {% if hat.work_enabled %}<label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_work_audience" value="true" required> I understand future approved autonomous Work will also receive this hat identity text.</label>{% endif %}
    <button type="submit">Save hat description and identity</button>
  </form>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/summary">
    <label>Short role summary <input name="short_summary" maxlength="160" value="{{ (hat.short_summary or '') | e }}" placeholder="Describe this role in one sentence"></label>
    <p class="form-hint">Shown alongside this hat's name to all conversations and authorized Work wearing <em>any</em> hat. Existing purposes were not copied into this field. Leave it empty to remove it; this summary is descriptive, not an instruction or permission.</p>
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_bear_audience" value="true" required> I understand every hat and authorized Work can see this short summary.</label>
    <button type="submit">Save short summary</button>
  </form>
  <details><summary>Preview compiled hat identity and directory</summary><pre>{{ identity_preview | e }}</pre></details>
  {% if previous_instructions %}
  <details>
    <summary>Review older stance instructions before transferring identity</summary>
    <p class="form-hint">These are effective legacy stance sources; hat-bound turns do not select them. Read them for identity or responsibility wording you want to rewrite in this hat. Do not copy tool, approval, or sandbox claims into hat identity: those limits come from verified runtime policy.</p>
    {% for instruction in previous_instructions %}
    <details>
      <summary>{{ instruction.profile | e }} · {{ instruction.source | e }}</summary>
      <pre>{{ instruction.content | e }}</pre>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </details>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="form-hint">The hat limits the Bear's work; it does not grant authority. An IDE conversation can choose a different hat only before its first interaction; after that, its hat is fixed.</p>
  <p><strong>IDE default for this Bear:</strong> {% if ide_default_hat_name %}{{ ide_default_hat_name | e }}{% else %}None selected{% endif %}</p>
  {% if not is_ide_default %}<form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/ide-default"><button type="submit">Make IDE default</button></form>{% endif %}
  <p class="form-hint">New IDE conversations wear the default before their first turn; existing conversations and Jobs are unchanged. /hat can choose another hat only as the first interaction.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/conversations">
    <button type="submit">Start a conversation wearing this hat</button>
  </form>
  <p class="form-hint">Notes from that conversation stay there unless Curate publishes a newly written fact to this hat. Shared hat knowledge is available to future conversations and eligible Job runs wearing it.</p>
  <p><a href="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/review">Review private notes for this hat →</a></p>
  <p><a href="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/legacy-review">Inspect and reauthor unattributed legacy notes →</a></p>
  <p><a href="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/core-review">Review this hat's knowledge for Bear-wide core →</a></p>
</div>
<div class="box">
  <h3>Permitted work surfaces</h3>
  <p class="form-hint">Only surfaces already assigned to this Bear are available. A hat narrows that grant; the person, channel or armature, and Job must still be authorized. Removing a surface also revokes that hat's Work eligibility for existing runs.</p>
  {% if choices %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/surfaces">
    {% for surface in choices %}
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="surface_ids" value="{{ surface.id }}"{% if surface.selected %} checked{% endif %}> {{ surface.name | e }}{% if surface.description %} — {{ surface.description | e }}{% endif %}</label>
    {% endfor %}
    <button type="submit">Save permitted surfaces</button>
  </form>
  {% else %}<p>No work surfaces are assigned to this Bear yet.</p>{% endif %}
</div>
<div class="box">
  <h3>Den web tool and host policy</h3>
  <p class="form-hint">A conversation wearing this hat can fetch an exact HTTPS host only when both the web-fetch tool and that host are granted. The current human must own the conversation; Den still applies block rules and public-DNS checks. Native Pair web fetches skip the ACP prompt only while this hat has both the fetch-tool and exact-host grants; an authorized Bear admin can also create that pair from a persistent ACP exact-host option, while others may choose a one-time approval. For a newly provisioned eligible Job sandbox, this hat's host grants are intersected with its assigned work surface's hosts by a provider that supports per-run ceilings; old or unreachable providers prevent hat-bound Work from starting; this does not authorize or start a Job, add a credential, or let a disconnected armature use local tools. Den requests cancellation of an active Work run on its next worker poll when this grant is revoked and retries provider teardown if it fails. Existing relays may remain reachable until that teardown succeeds; stop the run and check provider health if immediate isolation is needed. Old Bear-wide approvals do not carry into this hat. Search sends the query to an external provider: it requires its own tool grant and the exact provider host <code>api.search.brave.com</code>, not a web-fetch tool grant. Search uses a separately configured server-side provider key and may incur network, privacy, and usage costs; Jobs and other providers do not inherit this permission.</p>
  {% if web_grants.fetch_tool_grant_id %}
  <p>Web-fetch tool: granted</p>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <input type="hidden" name="grant_id" value="{{ web_grants.fetch_tool_grant_id }}">
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="revoke">Revoke web-fetch tool grant</button>
  </form>
  {% else %}
  <p>Web-fetch tool: not granted</p>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_future_job_audience" value="true" required> I understand this is shared with future conversations and eligible Job runs wearing this hat, once their separate execution and network policies permit it.</label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="enable_fetch">Grant web-fetch tool to this hat</button>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
  {% if web_grants.search_tool_grant_id %}
  <p>Web-search tool: granted</p>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <input type="hidden" name="grant_id" value="{{ web_grants.search_tool_grant_id }}">
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="revoke">Revoke web-search tool grant</button>
  </form>
  {% else %}
  <p>Web-search tool: not granted</p>
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_future_job_audience" value="true" required> I understand search queries may be sent to the configured provider using its server-side key, with usage costs, and this grant is shared with future conversations and eligible Job runs wearing this hat once their separate policies allow it.</label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="enable_search">Grant web-search tool to this hat</button>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
  <h4>Exact HTTPS hosts</h4>
  {% if web_grants.hosts %}
  <ul>{% for grant in web_grants.hosts %}
    <li>{{ grant.host | e }}
      <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
        <input type="hidden" name="grant_id" value="{{ grant.id }}">
        <button type="submit" name="action" value="revoke">Revoke {{ grant.host | e }}</button>
      </form>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>
  {% else %}<p>No HTTPS hosts granted.</p>{% endif %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <label>Exact HTTPS host <input name="host" placeholder="docs.example.com" required></label>
    <p class="form-hint">No wildcards, IP addresses, custom ports, HTTP, site accounts, or URL patterns. A host grant does not imply a tool grant.</p>
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_future_job_audience" value="true" required> I understand future conversations and eligible Job runs wearing this hat may use this host where their separate execution and work-surface policies allow it.</label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="allow_host">Grant HTTPS host</button>
  </form>
</div>
<div class="box">
  <h3>Editor workspace read permissions</h3>
  <p class="form-hint">A grant here covers only the selected read-only file action in the exact editor workspace root. It can be reused by future conversations wearing this hat, including other Bear members. Den checks the current member, conversation owner, hat, and grant on each use; the connected editor must also keep the requested path inside its live workspace and apply local sensitive-file rules. It does not grant terminal commands, writes, credentials, web access, or a Job. A Job with its own approved armature may use the grant only where all its other restrictions allow it.</p>
  {% if workspace_read_grants %}
  <ul>{% for grant in workspace_read_grants %}
    <li>{{ grant.title | e }} in <code>{{ grant.workspace_root | e }}</code>
      <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
        <input type="hidden" name="grant_id" value="{{ grant.id }}">
        <button type="submit" name="action" value="revoke_workspace">Revoke this workspace read permission</button>
      </form>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>
  {% else %}<p>No editor workspace read permissions granted.</p>{% endif %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/access">
    <label>Read-only action <select name="tool_name" required>
      {% for choice in workspace_read_choices %}<option value="{{ choice.provider_name | e }}">{{ choice.title | e }}</option>{% endfor %}
    </select></label>
    <label>Exact editor workspace root <input name="workspace_root" placeholder="/workspace/project" required maxlength="2000" autocomplete="off"></label>
    <p class="form-hint">Use the absolute, normalized root reported by the connected editor. The saved permission applies only to the selected action in that root and does not override local filesystem policy. Do not include <code>..</code>, wildcards, a home-directory shortcut, or a trailing slash. An existing approval for a different root will not match.</p>
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_future_job_audience" value="true" required> I understand this permission can be reused by every authorized member's future conversations wearing this hat and by eligible Jobs only if they have their own connected, bounded work surface.</label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="grant_workspace_read">Grant workspace read action</button>
  </form>
</div>
<div class="box">
  <h3>Automatic memory sharing for this hat: {{ hat.auto_curate_enabled and "on" or "off" }}</h3>
  <p class="form-hint">When enabled, Curate may read a private note from a conversation wearing this hat, send it through this Bear's configured model provider, and publish a newly written fact to the hat. All Bear members and eligible Job runs wearing the hat, now or in the future, may read it. Model inference may have privacy, network, and usage costs. Curate does not publish the note verbatim, but its rewrite cannot guarantee that sensitive details or prompt injections are removed. Shared knowledge remains untrusted data; this setting grants no tools, credentials, permissions, or Job authority.</p>
  {% if hat.auto_curate_enabled %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/auto-curate"><button type="submit" name="action" value="disable">Disable automatic sharing</button></form>
  {% else %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/auto-curate">
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_audience" value="true" required> I understand private notes may be sent to the configured model, and rewritten knowledge becomes available to every member and authorized Job run wearing this hat.</label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="enable">Enable automatic sharing</button>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
</div>
<div class="box">
  <h3>Use in Jobs: {{ hat.work_enabled and "on" or "off" }}</h3>
  <p class="form-hint">When enabled, eligible Job runs wearing this hat can use its identity and curated memory, including facts learned later. Enabling Job use does not start a run or grant tools, credentials, or access; each run still needs an authorized Job and permitted surfaces. Existing hat memory is reviewed when enabling Job use, not before every run or new fact.</p>
  {% if hat.work_enabled %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/work"><button type="submit" name="action" value="disable">Disable Job use</button></form>
  {% else %}
  <form method="post" action="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/work">
    <input type="hidden" name="expected_identity_sha256" value="{{ identity_sha256 | e }}">
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm_identity_audience" value="true" required> I reviewed the identity text above for autonomous Work in an untrusted workspace.</label>
    <label>Type <code>enable work</code> to confirm <input name="confirmation" autocomplete="off" required></label>
    <button type="submit" name="action" value="enable"{% if grant_count == 0 or historical_hat_records > 0 %} disabled{% endif %}>Enable Work for an empty hat</button>
  </form>
  {% endif %}
  {% if historical_hat_records > 0 %}<p><a href="/bear/{{ bear.slug | e }}/hats/{{ hat.id }}/work-review">Review {{ historical_hat_records }} historical hat record{% if historical_hat_records != 1 %}s{% endif %} before enabling Work →</a></p>{% endif %}
  {% if work_reviews %}
  <details><summary>Past Work memory reviews ({{ work_reviews | length }})</summary>
    <ul>{% for review in work_reviews %}
      <li>{{ review.reviewed_at | e }} · {{ review.reviewed_by | e }} reviewed {{ review.record_count }} record{% if review.record_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}: {{ review.rationale | e }} <code>{{ review.id }}</code>{% if review.identity_sha256 %} · identity fingerprint <code>{{ review.identity_sha256 | e }}</code>{% endif %}</li>
    {% endfor %}</ul>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
